0..78 Comment "// Two migrations to one world, a value held at the seat and read there again."
79..81 Comment "//"
82..159 Comment "// It witnesses a capture crossing in: the second migration\'s body reads what"
160..190 Comment "// the first held at the seat."
191..193 Comment "//"
194..270 Comment "// The first migration holds a value at the seat and brings its handle back."
271..347 Comment "// `leta` opens the handle at the operator\'s world, and the second migration"
348..427 Comment "// reads what it binds at the seat. In one process a handle is its content, and"
428..483 Comment "// each crossing, in or back, is a commit then a deref."
484..486 Comment "//"
487..562 Comment "// - see: Murphy, Crary and Harper, \"Type-Safe Distributed Programming with"
563..588 Comment "//   ML5\", TGC 2007, § 3"
589..653 Comment "// - see: Rainey et al., \"LoCalMem\", PACMPL 10 (ICFP 2026), § 5"
654..717 Comment "// - see: `open.gandr` — what crosses back from one migration"
719..785 Comment "// The operator\'s and the seat\'s worlds, each declaration\'s entry."
